Room Monitor v7.3 regression strategy
=====================================

The firmware depends on ESP32/Arduino/BSEC hardware libraries, so the default
CI gate combines host-side source regression checks with real PlatformIO
firmware and SPIFFS compilation.

Run locally from the project root:

    python tools/validate_project.py
    python tools/check_inline_js.py
    platformio run
    platformio run -t buildfs

The static checks cover NVS key limits, v7.3 UI/version consistency, duplicate
HTML IDs, diagnostics/navigation presence, secret-free configuration export,
legacy MQTT command compatibility, CSRF markers, verified OTA markers, and
watchdog/diagnostics wiring. GitHub Actions performs the same checks and then
compiles both ESP32 artifacts.

Hardware-in-loop acceptance still needs a real Room Monitor for sensor input,
Wi-Fi recovery, MQTT/TLS broker connectivity, OTA reboot confirmation, and
factory-reset behavior.
